# Maven build output, including target/pit-reports and target/surefire-reports. The differential
# harness writes its long-form report to target/harness/report.txt, which is generated and therefore
# lands here rather than being committed.
target/

# The differential harness's unpacked OUTPUT: readable copies of the frozen corpus and the filesystem
# tree, tens of megabytes, rebuilt by `node harness/unpack-fixtures.cjs` in seconds.
#
# harness/fixtures/ is NOT here and must not be. It is the frozen JavaScript answers themselves — the
# only surviving record of a service that was deleted — plus the catalogue the test asserts against.
# Losing it would not be an inconvenience: there is nothing left to regenerate it from. See
# harness/README.md.
harness/out/

# The long-form report, if a run writes one here rather than into target/. It is GENERATED — the
# catalogue in harness/fixtures/expected.json is the asserted artefact — and a committed copy is worse
# than none: this one sat in the tree for weeks saying DIVERGENT 745 while the catalogue said 833, and
# two READMEs quoted the stale number as fact. DifferentialHarnessTest already says in writing that it
# is not committed; this is what makes that true.
harness/report.txt
